.TH RASDAEMON 8 "@META_DATE@" "@META_ALIAS@" "RAS event logging daemon"

.SH NAME
rasdaemon \- monitor and log Linux RAS events

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rasdaemon
[\fIOPTION\fR]...

.SH DESCRIPTION

The \fBrasdaemon\fR program monitors Reliability, Availability and
Serviceability (RAS) reports exposed as Linux kernel trace events. It prefers
tracefs and falls back to the legacy debugfs tracing directory. Decoded events
are reported through syslog or journald and can optionally be stored using a
compiled SQLite, MySQL/MariaDB, or PostgreSQL backend.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B "--usage"
Display a brief usage message and exit.
.TP
.B "--help"
Display a help message and exit.
.TP
.BR "-d" ", " "--disable"
Disable RAS tracing events and exit.
.TP
.BR "-e" ", " "--enable"
Enable RAS tracing events and exit.
.TP
.BI "-c " FNAME ", " "--config=" FNAME
Read environment settings from \fIFNAME\fR instead of
@RASDAEMON_ENV@.
.TP
.BR "-f" ", " "--foreground"
Run in the foreground and print events on the console. This is useful for
testing and for service managers. If not specified, the program runs in daemon
mode.
.TP
.BR "-r" ", " "--record"
Record RAS events using the selected SQL backend. The backend defaults to
SQLite and can be selected with \fBRASDAEMON_DB_BACKEND\fR. At least one
database backend must have been compiled in.
.TP
.BR "-i" ", " "--ipmitool"
Enable ipmitool logging. This option is present only when OpenBMC unified SEL
support was compiled in.
.TP
.BR "-p" ", " "--post-processing"
Decode an x86 machine-check event from raw register values instead of starting
the daemon. This option and the following machine-check options are present
only when x86 MCE support was compiled in.
.TP
.B "--smca"
Decode an AMD SMCA event.
.TP
.BI "--model=" MODEL
Set the CPU model used for offline decoding.
.TP
.BI "--family=" FAMILY
Set the CPU family used for offline decoding.
.TP
.BI "--bank=" BANK_NUM
Set the machine-check bank number.
.TP
.BI "--ipid=" IPID_REG
Set the IPID register value for AMD SMCA decoding.
.TP
.BI "--status=" STATUS_REG
Set the machine-check status register value.
.TP
.BI "--synd=" SYNDROME_REG
Set the AMD SMCA syndrome register value.
.TP
.B "--version"
Print the program version and exit.

.SH CONFIG FILE

The \fBrasdaemon\fR program reads environment settings from
@RASDAEMON_ENV@ by default. The general format is
\fINAME=value\fR. Values already present in the process environment take
precedence over the file. Runtime reload is not supported.

\fBRASDAEMON_DB_BACKEND\fR selects \fBsqlite3\fR, \fBmysql\fR, or
\fBpostgresql\fR. \fBRASDAEMON_HOSTNAME\fR overrides the hostname recorded by
remote database backends. Backend-specific connection settings, event-disable
syntax, action thresholds, and trigger variables are documented in the
installed configuration file.

.SH LOG LEVEL

Each log entry has a level prefix that describes the severity of the log to
help users determine which logs are more valuable. Currently, three levels are
used:

.TP
.B "ALERT"
An uncorrected hardware error has been handled but may have caused side
effects.
.TP
.B "CRIT"
An uncorrected hardware error has been detected.
.TP
.B "ERROR"
A corrected hardware error has been detected.

.SH SEE ALSO
\fBras-mc-ctl\fR(8)
